From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruiyangke <me@ry.ke>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] popup: Keep popups and dialogs clear of the system's insets

On an iPad the status bar, the home indicator and the on-screen keyboard
cover the window's edges, but popups were placed, and dialogs padded, only
for window decorations. A menu opened near the bottom edge slid under the
keyboard, and a dialog's edge sat under the status bar.

`system_insets` reports what the system draws over the window (the safe
area, and the keyboard where it is larger than the bottom inset); desktop
windows report none. The positioner adds it to the frame it keeps popups
inside, and `Dialog` adds it to its window paddings. `add_edges` sums two
sets of insets.

Remove when upstream keeps popups and dialogs inside the window's safe area.
---
